course: dictionary
lesson: 12303
title: Cordless
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A cordless machine works without a wire running from it to the wall. «The cordless drill made a hole in the wall in seconds.» The word is made of cord, a wire, and less, meaning without. So cordless means without a wire.
explain: Most cordless machines run on a battery, so you can carry them around the house. But a battery runs out, so you must charge it first. «The cordless vacuum cleaner stopped halfway, because its battery was flat.»
explain: Look for clues. If a sentence talks about charging, or carrying something around with no wire attached, the word is about having no wire. Check your meaning by swapping in "without a wire" and reading the sentence again.
fact: Cordless means works without a wire plugged into the wall.
fact: «Cordless» is built from «cord», a wire, and «-less», meaning without.
fact: Most cordless devices run on a battery, so they must be charged.
fact: A cordless kettle has a jug you lift off its base; the base is still plugged into the wall.
fact: «Cordless» is an adjective and does not change form, so we never say "more cordless".
exercise: «Dad used a cordless drill to hang the shelf.» What does cordless mean here? | It is very loud | *It works without a wire to the wall | It only works in the garden | It is made of cord and very long
exercise: «The cordless phone rang, so Ana carried it from the hall to the lounge.» Why could Ana carry the phone so easily? | *It has no wire to the wall, so she could move it | It was a toy | It was very heavy | It was broken
exercise: Which of these is a cordless device? | A toaster with a long wire that plugs into the wall | A lamp that must stay plugged in at all times | *A vacuum cleaner that runs on a battery with no wire
test:
«After the cordless vacuum cleaner ran out of battery, Sam had to charge it.» Why did Sam charge it? | To make it lighter | *Because it runs on a battery that needs charging | Because it was too heavy to lift | Because it was broken | To make it louder
What does cordless mean? | Has no buttons | Is always wet | *Works without a wire plugged into the wall | Makes a loud noise when it is switched on
exam:
«The cordless kettle's jug sat on its base, which was plugged into the wall.» What does cordless tell us about the jug? | It must stay on the base all the time | It needs a longer wire to work | It is made of cord | *It can be lifted off its base without a wire joining it
